# TDD WORKFLOW AUTOMATION DIRECTIVE [ACTIVE]

## NEXT FILE TO READ
After processing this directive file, the AI must:
1. CHECK WORKING CONTEXT: Read `/Users/robertthiel/DevHead_LLC/RisingPunk/rules/context/tdd/active-working-context.mdc`
2. DETERMINE NEXT STEP based on the working context status markers
3. ONLY THEN proceed to the AI Directive Tree if appropriate

## DIRECTIVE KEY
- [to-do]: Task not yet started
- [in-progress]: Task currently being worked on
- [done]: Task completed
- [blocked]: Task cannot proceed (requires attention)
- {Make File: path}: Create/modify file at specified path
- {Run Script: path}: Execute script at specified path
- {FeatureName}: Replace with actual feature name
- {SubFeatureName}: Replace with actual sub-feature name

## DIRECTIVE PURPOSE
Guide AI through TDD workflow systematically without requiring explicit instructions for each step.

## ACTION PROTOCOL
1. CHECK: On each interaction, first check `/Users/robertthiel/DevHead_LLC/RisingPunk/rules/context/tdd/active-working-context.mdc` for current state
2. DECIDE: 
   - If any step is [in-progress], continue from that position
   - If all steps are [to-do], then consult the AI Directive Tree and start with Reset Context
3. IDENTIFY: Locate current position in workflow tree (find [to-do] OR [in-progress] tasks)
4. UPDATE: Change status from [to-do] → [in-progress] → [done] as tasks complete
5. EXECUTE: Run required scripts at each workflow position automatically
6. PROGRESS: Move to next step only when current step is fully complete
7. REPORT: Clearly state current position and next action in the workflow

## WORKING MODE
- MINIMIZE QUESTIONS: Proceed through workflow with minimal user prompting
- EXECUTE SCRIPTS: Run all scripts specified in the workflow tree without requiring permission
- AUTOMATIC UPDATES: Update status markers in context files without explicit instructions
- TRACK ALL FEATURES: For each feature, process all sub-features systematically

## NOTIFICATION REQUIREMENT
- IF WORKFLOW IS BLOCKED: Immediately notify user with specific reason
- IF FILES ARE MISSING: Automatically create required files and continue
- IF PATHS DON'T MATCH: Notify user that paths in directive tree need updating
- IF OUT OF ALIGNMENT: Tell user "WORKFLOW ALIGNMENT ERROR: [specific issue]" and suggest fix

## PERSISTENCE PROTOCOL
- MAINTAIN CONTEXT: Ensure all status changes are recorded in context files
- FEATURE TRACKING: Keep track of all features and their implementation status
- CONTEXT CONTINUITY: Maintain workflow position between sessions

## THE-PLAN INTEGRATION
This directive implements @the-plan.mdc principles:
- Execute requests immediately, don't just discuss them
- Follow requests exactly without adding extras
- Stay focused on one task at a time
- Keep implementation simple
- Verify completion of each step with evidence
- Document changes properly

## CONTEXT MANAGEMENT
- MONITOR SIZE: AI should monitor context file size to ensure it fits within available context window
- SIZE LIMITS: Follow size directives in active-working-context.mdc comment header
- ARCHIVE SCRIPT: Use `/Users/robertthiel/DevHead_LLC/RisingPunk/rules/tdd/scripts/manage-context-size.sh` to manage overflow
- NOTIFICATION: When context approaches size limits, notify user with specific warnings
- ARCHIVING: When necessary, archive older history entries while preserving recent and active items
- USER ALERT: If context overflow may impact AI performance, alert user immediately

